Wrap bootloader_init() sub-stages + SOURCE-LEVEL exception capture hooks (v9)

arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_boot_hb_wrap.c (new, rewritten)
arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/hal.mk
arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_start.c
arch/xtensa/src/common/xtensa_vectors.S

WHY v9 (runs 83/84/85: runtime IRAM rewrites do not work here)
--------------------------------------------------------------
v6 hooked the user-exception slot and v7 hooked ALL 15 vector slots at
runtime; neither ever captured anything (35 boots each), while the storm
kept running the ORIGINAL handlers (Saved PC inside _xtensa_context_save)
-- the slot stores never took effect.  v8 additionally hooked
_xtensa_panic: the boot then died inside the arm probe itself (audit
never written, the >0 marker gone), i.e. that store faults outright
while the slot stores are silently dropped.  Conclusion: no runtime
writes to the vector region at all.

v9 changes:
- xtensa_vectors.S: the level2/level3/nmi/kernel/user vectors now call
  hb_exc_stub_180/1c0/2c0/300/340 and the double-exception vector body
  is collapsed into a call0 hb_exc_stub_3c0 -- link-time symbol
  resolution, zero runtime writes.  Window vectors untouched.
- esp32s3_boot_hb_wrap.c: hb_arm_exc_probe no longer writes anywhere;
  it only reads back the live vecbase for the [HB] ARM health line.
  hb_dump_prev re-arms hb_exc_area[0] after dumping (the bss-clearing
  bootloader stage never runs in this debug configuration, so the asm
  guard would otherwise see cold-boot garbage and skip every capture).
- Boot-stage heartbeat probes and the v5 ROM-stack switch kept.

Debug-only change; probes to be reverted once boot is verified.

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_boot_hb_wrap.c b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_boot_hb_wrap.c
